1. James reads 3 pages in 10 minutes.
2. We can find the rate at which James reads by dividing the number of pages read by the time taken: rate = 3 pages / 10 minutes.
3. James reads 18 pages. To find out how long it takes him to read 18 pages, we can set up a proportion:
   $\frac{3 \text{ pages}}{10 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{18 \text{ pages}}{x \text{ minutes}}$
4. Cross-multiply: $3x = 10 \times 18$
5. $3x = 180$
6. Divide by 3: $x = \frac{180}{3} = 60$
7. It takes James 60 minutes to read 18 pages.

Alternatively, we can use the rate from step 2:
Time = $\frac{\text{Number of pages}}{\text{Rate}}$
Time = $\frac{18 \text{ pages}}{3 \text{ pages} / 10 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{18}{3/10} = 18 \times \frac{10}{3} = 6 \times 10 = 60$ minutes.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{60}$
